{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion primitives, separating sensor outcomes from action execution. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, deterministic recovery (turns or full_rotate only as last resort). Recovery states are one-shot and always return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to clarify uncontrollable vs controllable event flow.",
    "Specification automaton enforces: random_walk in clear, move_forward in short bursts, deterministic turn recovery after obstacles, and rapid return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
